    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"85c74583-d60a-402f-b2ac-8c1c5a018d38"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"fb1ad2c4-8f69-4019-8d07-\
10dde5e59c78"],

Cell["\<\
With tube radius 0 the only member is the reference, when excess 0 is \
allowed. With a wider tube, excess 0 may contain other shortest paths. Thus \
zero excess alone does not specify the reference.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9c1cd0c8-60cd-4451-9483-85d52600137c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is a geometric family of walks, not a homotopy class. Tube radius and \
excess are distinct from the edit width measured by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDeformationSize"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDeformationSize", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fbf22c2d-c2b3-4f91-8063-41a71a3cd3b6"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fa5cd3b9-dd01-400c-b7ee-37e3907bb8f6"],

Cell["\<\
On a bipartite substrate every edge changes distance from the source by one. \
Consequently every forward member is a shortest path: positive exact excess \
gives an empty family, and increasing an upper excess bound adds nothing. \
This includes square grids. The object therefore does not describe general \
length-increasing detours of a shortest path.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d0c25f55-999f-49fb-b73a-c24972f455e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Closeness to the reference also does not certify a local deformation. On a \
six-cycle the two opposite shortest routes can belong to the same radius-1 \
tube although no triangle or square move connects them. Use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraHomotopy"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraHomotopy", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d42cef53-089d-498d-be0c-866d4c2d0bb9"],
 " when a certificate in a specified face relation is required."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9740989b-0589-4203-8b3f-4aa7687753c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "588c8868-38a2-4035-8d5d-8c6c3a7ff058"],
 " reading is a list of pruned directed acyclic graphs on states {",
 StyleBox["step", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["vertex", "TI"],
 "}, one for each attainable allowed excess. Paths in these graphs correspond \
exactly to the walks. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6ae078d-8e3a-4bdc-913c-88540addbe42"],
 " counts them without enumerating them. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce1de31-13ef-42cb-b374-797ee5fa26da"],
 " gives the attainable edge lengths, as a scalar when there is only one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"665815ad-b8cb-443e-ba9b-c9b1214fc6b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<VertexDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "be4f12aa-ba21-487a-b51f-fa86632f864f"],
 " is the number of visits to each substrate vertex summed over all members. \
Repeated visits count repeatedly. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f79cdc74-1813-402c-8793-50fa1db8af45"],
 " counts directed edge traversals, with keys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"DirectedEdge", "[", 
   RowBox[{"u", ",", "v"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d65659c5-4983-4b05-a5cf-42a75e5a699a"],
 ". Both readings project the position graphs back to substrate vertices and \
edges without enumerating members."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"37805f39-4281-4f35-b04c-5461ee45d538"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de3f99f1-1321-46a8-b5ce-95073f64033c"],
 " reads ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e05f1c7-7732-42f6-a25d-5d2abc327682"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "acabff88-ae0b-41c5-ae67-12b2130cc0d9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab9cd125-0b65-4c14-bc29-48b2c2151a64"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<VertexDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e1f5e71e-5cad-4cdc-a1fc-34ff5bf7b917"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37292cce-2be9-49b3-8395-20ed890cd47f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Subgraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e1cd0aa-cf73-42f5-a100-eb8358e90678"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CountingMeasure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c829cbe-a533-4c8f-98d3-50e8985f61c6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<RiemannianMeasure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f61820c-3c6f-40be-a5b6-086437cd9787"],
 ". The last three use the support of the family, with the usual \
region-measure conventions of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ad49b5e9-1f94-41eb-8cab-1e1eea354d36"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2c2401a3-ded5-406a-98ef-91e3780fe266"],

Cell["\<\
For a finite excess bound, counting uses a finite layered graph and is \
polynomial in its size. Listing all members can still require exponential \
output.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"71114b82-fcbf-4242-8d71-a86fbaac6092"]
}, Open  ]],

